\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\insrsid11822444\charrsid11822444 Halo is superimposed on a model containing about 500 polygons, and the material shader itself consists of two rings, each with its own color. 
\par Basically, by manipulating with these colors, you will achieve the effect you want.
\par The first ring is closer to the sun and has a brighter color, the second is farther and darker, however this is at your discretion, all the settings are in front of you.
\par 
\par 3.1
\par halo ring 1 - first ring energy effect
\par 
\par 3.2
\par Halo ring 1 color - this is the HDR color, by clicking on which you will see the color palette can be changed by the circular slider, 
\par the color saturation changes in the square field, the RGB drop-down list, and the R,G,B sliders  we don't need it either.
\par you mai play with A slider, but i dont do it. Intensity has a strong impact on the overall picture.
\par 
\par 3.3
\par Halo Ring 1 size - controls the size of the inner halo ring
\par 
\par 3.3.1
\par Halo Ring 1 intensity - Inner ring intensity
\par 
\par 3.3.2
\par Halo Ring 1 strenght  -Inner ring strenght
\par 
\par 
\par 3.4
\par Halo ring 2 = second ring energy effect
\par 
\par 3.5
\par Halo ring str - Outer ring strenght
\par 
\par 3.6
\par Halo Ring 2 thickness - thickness of outer ring
\par 
\par 3.7
\par Halo Ring 2 color - this is the HDR color, by clicking on which you will see the color palette can be changed by the circular slider, 
\par the color saturation changes in the square field, the RGB drop-down list, and the R,G,B sliders  we don't need it either.
\par you mai play with A slider, but i dont do it. Intensity has a strong impact on the overall picture.
\par 
\par 3.8 
\par Halo Ring 2 Size - Size of outer ring
\par 
\par 3.9
\par Halo Ring 2 intensity - outer ring intensity
\par 
\par 4.0
\par Halo Ring 2 width - width of outer ring
\par 
\par 5.0 textures are not compressed you must choise you prefer compression metod.
\par 
\par 
\par 
